  output            dst_adc_enable;
  output            dst_adc_valid;
  output  [15:0]    dst_adc_data;

endmodule
```

The `control` port is a 32-bit input that controls the operation of the module. Bit 0 is used to enable or disable the module. Bit 1 is used to enable or disable the ADC. All other bits are reserved and should be set to 0.

The `status` port is a 32-bit output that reports the status of the module. The module ID is encoded in bits 23:0. The module ID for this module is 0xA0.

The `src_adc_enable` port is a single-bit input that controls whether or not the ADC is enabled.

The `src_adc_valid` port is a single-bit input that indicates whether or not the ADC has valid data.

The `src_adc_data` port is a 16-bit input that contains the data from the ADC.

The `dst_adc_enable` port is a single-bit output that controls whether or not the ADC is enabled.

The `dst_adc_valid` port is a single-bit output that indicates whether or not the module has valid data.

The `dst_adc_data` port is a 16-bit output that contains the data from the ADC.

Your task is to implement the `adc_fifo` module that satisfies the above requirements. Your implementation should be contained within a single Verilog module that is no more than 200 lines long.

