In this problem, you are given a Verilog module named `crc` that implements a cyclic redundancy check (CRC) algorithm. The module takes in a single bit of data (`data_in`), a clock signal (`clk`), a reset signal (`rst`), and a CRC enable signal (`crc_en`). The module outputs a 16-bit CRC value (`crc_out`).

The CRC algorithm is implemented using a linear feedback shift register (LFSR) with a polynomial of `x^16 + x^15 + x^2 + 1`. The LFSR is initialized to all zeros when the reset signal is high. When the CRC enable signal is high, the LFSR is updated with each clock cycle using the following polynomial coefficients:

```
lfsr_c[0] = lfsr_q[15] ^ data_in[0];
lfsr_c[1] = lfsr_q[0];
lfsr_c[2] = lfsr_q[1] ^ lfsr_q[15] ^ data_in[0];
lfsr_c[3] = lfsr_q[2];
lfsr_c[4] = lfsr_q[3];
lfsr_c[5] = lfsr_q[4];
lfsr_c[6] = lfsr_q[5];
