You are tasked with designing a UART module in Verilog that can transmit data at a specified baud rate. The module should have an external clock input and an output line for transmitting data. The UART should be able to transmit a single byte of data at a time and should be able to handle transmitting data continuously.

The UART module should have a reset input that is active high. When the reset input is high, the UART should reset all its internal registers and stop transmitting data.

