In digital design, a D flip-flop is a fundamental building block that stores a single bit of information. It takes in a data input (D) and a clock signal (CLK), and on each rising edge of the clock, the output (Q) changes to the value of D. A D flip-flop can be implemented using logic gates, such as the sky130_fd_sc_ms__dlxtp_1 module shown below.

```
module sky130_fd_sc_ms__dlxtp_1 (
