        .D(D),
        .GATE(GATE),
        .VPWR(VPWR),
        .VGND(VGND),
        .VPB(VPB),
        .VNB(VNB)
    );

endmodule
```

In this module, Q represents the output, D represents the data input, and GATE, VPWR, VGND, VPB, and VNB are control signals.

Your task is to implement a 4-bit D flip-flop register using the sky130_fd_sc_ms__dlxtp_1 module. Your implementation should have a single clock input (CLK), a single reset input (RST), a single enable input (EN), a single 4-bit data input (D), and a single 4-bit output (Q). On each rising edge of CLK, the output should update to the value of D, provided that EN is high and RST is low. When RST is high, the output should be cleared to 0.

You should implement your solution within a single module, using no more than 200 lines of Verilog code.

