Instruction:
In digital circuit design, a buffer is a logic gate that takes an input signal and produces an output signal that is the same as the input signal. The Verilog code snippet below shows a module for a buffer.

```
module sky130_fd_sc_hvl__buf (
    X,
    A
);

    // Module ports
    output X;
    input  A;

    // Module supplies
    supply1 VPWR;
    supply0 VGND;
