Instruction:
You are tasked with designing a verilog module that takes in two 8-bit inputs, `A` and `B`, and outputs the sum of the two inputs, `S`. The module should also have a carry output, `C`, which is set to 1 if the sum of any two corresponding bits in `A` and `B` results in a carry. For example, if `A` is `8'b10101010` and `B` is `8'b01010101`, the output should be `S = 16'b11111111` and `C = 1`.

Use the following module template to implement your design:

```
module adder_8bit (
    A,
    B,
    S,
    C
);

    input [7:0] A;
    input [7:0] B;
    output reg [7:0] S;
    output reg C;

    // Add your code here

endmodule
```

You can use the `sky130_fd_sc_hd__xor2_1` and `sky130_fd_sc_hd__and2_1` modules from the Skywater 130nm process to implement your design. The `xor2` module takes in two inputs and outputs the exclusive OR of the inputs. The `and2` module takes in two inputs and outputs the AND of the inputs.

Response:
module adder_8bit (
    A,
    B,
    S,
    C
);

    input [7:0] A;
    input [7:0] B;
    output reg [7:0] S;
    output reg C;

    // Generate the sum bits
    genvar i;
    generate
        for (i = 0; i < 8; i = i + 1) begin
            sky130_fd_sc_hd__xor2_1 xor (
                .X(A[i]),
                .Y(B[i]),
                .Z(S[i])
            );
        end
    endgenerate

    // Generate the carry bits
    genvar j;
    reg [7:0] carry;
    generate
        for (j = 0; j < 7; j = j + 1) begin
            sky130_fd_sc_hd__and2_1 and (
                .A(A[j]),
                .B(B[j]),
                .X(carry[j+1])
            );
        end
    endgenerate

    // Set the carry output
    assign C = carry[7];

    // Add the carry to the sum
    always @(*) begin
        if (C) begin
            S <= A + B + 1;
        end else begin
            S <= A + B;
        end
    end

endmodule

